1
00:01:04,230 --> 00:01:05,982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

2
00:01:09,694 --> 00:01:13,031
{\an8}DAUGHTER OF YANG GWAN-SIK AND OH AE-SUN
YANG GEUM-MYEONG! ACCEPTED TO SNU!

3
00:01:20,163 --> 00:01:23,583
{\an8}'88 SEOUL OLYMPICS CELEBRATION
ADVANCED CITIZENS! ADVANCED STREETS!

4
00:01:23,666 --> 00:01:25,627
{\an8}Who cares
if you're from the Olympics?

5
00:01:25,710 --> 00:01:27,712
{\an8}<i>Haenyeo </i>do more than Olympians every day!

6
00:01:27,796 --> 00:01:29,214
<i>For the </i>haenyeo,

7
00:01:29,297 --> 00:01:32,133
<i>their "Olympics"</i>
<i>was simply making ends meet.</i>

8
00:01:32,217 --> 00:01:35,386
Please, everyone, calm down.
If you'd just let us explain.

9
00:01:35,470 --> 00:01:37,680
<i>And the Olympic events</i>
<i>they competed in</i>

10
00:01:37,764 --> 00:01:39,974
<i>were as grand as they were cruel.</i>

11
00:01:40,725 --> 00:01:41,976
<i>Games without medals,</i>

12
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:43,394
<i>pensions,</i>

13
00:01:43,978 --> 00:01:45,105
<i>or retirement.</i>

14
00:01:45,688 --> 00:01:48,024
What the hell are you ruining
our business for?

15
00:01:48,108 --> 00:01:50,902
Why? Go do your Olympics
if that's what you want.

16
00:01:50,985 --> 00:01:53,363
- Why do we have to sacrifice for it?
- Oh God.

17
00:01:53,947 --> 00:01:55,448
Who are you trying to punish here?

18
00:01:55,532 --> 00:01:58,201
Who ever saw a conch
protesting the Olympics?

19
00:01:58,284 --> 00:01:59,661
Or a fish blocking the roads?

20
00:01:59,744 --> 00:02:02,580
All right! Enough!

21
00:02:02,664 --> 00:02:04,624
Seriously! I've had enough.
We need to get through!

22
00:02:04,707 --> 00:02:06,376
How many times do I have to tell you?

23
00:02:06,459 --> 00:02:09,129
The Olympic torch
will be passing right through here!

24
00:02:09,212 --> 00:02:11,798
Americans are going to watch this
on their TVs!

25
00:02:11,881 --> 00:02:13,842
We can't let anyone see that.

26
00:02:13,925 --> 00:02:17,387
All these disgusting intestines
and the smell of fish guts here?

27
00:02:17,470 --> 00:02:19,597
Are you stupid or what?
Can you smell your TV?

28
00:02:19,681 --> 00:02:23,143
We have orders from the government
to clean up anything unsightly.

29
00:02:23,226 --> 00:02:24,727
That's an order!

30
00:02:24,811 --> 00:02:25,770
That's an order!

31
00:02:25,854 --> 00:02:27,730
- Why you little…
- Unsightly, eh?

32
00:02:27,814 --> 00:02:30,984
Now I've heard it all.
You're going to take away our livelihoods

33
00:02:31,067 --> 00:02:34,195
just to serve some Americans
thousands of miles away?

34
00:02:34,279 --> 00:02:36,739
Does that make
any kind of sense to you at all?

35
00:02:36,823 --> 00:02:39,159
Is that the American way
of doing business?

36
00:02:39,242 --> 00:02:41,953
Trampling the poor
by taking the food out of our mouths!

37
00:02:42,036 --> 00:02:42,996
I can't take this.

38
00:02:43,079 --> 00:02:45,206
Oh, come on,
you're no crusaders for justice.

39
00:02:45,290 --> 00:02:47,500
You're just fish-sellers like I am.

40
00:02:47,584 --> 00:02:50,044
I think we can all handle
a little loss for the greater good.

41
00:02:50,128 --> 00:02:52,046
Now stop messing things up!

42
00:02:52,130 --> 00:02:54,591
I know what happened.
They paid you off, didn't they?

43
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:58,094
What? 'Cause I don't have
enough money yet, you think?

44
00:02:58,178 --> 00:02:59,554
How much was it, huh?

45
00:02:59,637 --> 00:03:02,557
How much did they pay you
for our blood, sweat, and tears?

46
00:03:03,183 --> 00:03:04,642
You call yourself "chief"?

47
00:03:04,726 --> 00:03:07,228
Maybe you would have some manners
if you had gone to school.

48
00:03:07,312 --> 00:03:08,938
Explain it to us again!

49
00:03:09,022 --> 00:03:11,107
The Olympic torch will pass through
for a few minutes,

50
00:03:11,191 --> 00:03:13,985
and just for that,
you wanna take away our income?

51
00:03:14,068 --> 00:03:15,862
What kind of law is that?

52
00:03:15,945 --> 00:03:17,697
- Oh, please. What about it?
- Go away!

53
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:19,282
What do you know about the law?

54
00:03:19,365 --> 00:03:21,326
Oh Ae-sun!

55
00:03:21,409 --> 00:03:22,869
Where's Ae-sun?

56
00:03:22,952 --> 00:03:26,164
Go get our deputy chief.
She finished high school.

57
00:03:26,247 --> 00:03:28,374
Finished high school?

58
00:03:28,458 --> 00:03:31,419
- She didn't even graduate.
- Well, she went at least.

59
00:03:32,045 --> 00:03:34,380
Where is our deputy chief?

60
00:03:34,464 --> 00:03:37,133
- She would know exactly what to say!
- Ae-sun!

61
00:03:37,217 --> 00:03:39,469
What are you shouting about
Ae-sun for?

62
00:03:39,552 --> 00:03:41,930
It's not like she can do anything.

63
00:03:42,013 --> 00:03:45,350
I want you to explain
how not selling our fish helps the nation.

64
00:03:45,433 --> 00:03:47,727
God, can't you see this doesn't matter?

65
00:03:48,311 --> 00:03:50,271
If North Korea decides
to ruin our Olympics

66
00:03:50,355 --> 00:03:53,316
and bursts the Mount Kumgang dam,
all of Seoul will be flooded.

67
00:03:53,399 --> 00:03:56,027
Even the 63 Building
would be under the sea.

68
00:03:56,110 --> 00:03:57,987
Don't you follow the news?

69
00:03:58,071 --> 00:04:00,323
Don't you understand?
It's for the greater good.

70
00:04:00,406 --> 00:04:03,701
Compared to history,
your little lives don't matter at all.

71
00:04:03,785 --> 00:04:05,578
Yes, they do. Yes, they do.

72
00:04:05,662 --> 00:04:07,622
- You bet your ass they matter.
- Oh, it's hopeless.

73
00:04:10,124 --> 00:04:12,710
Do you know how riots get started?

74
00:04:12,794 --> 00:04:15,546
If you kick over a dog's bowl of food,

75
00:04:15,630 --> 00:04:18,466
it's gonna start shitting
all over the place!

76
00:04:18,549 --> 00:04:19,759
- Is that what you want?
- Let go.

77
00:04:19,842 --> 00:04:21,052
Is that what you want?

78
00:04:21,636 --> 00:04:22,553
Huh?

79
00:04:22,637 --> 00:04:23,680
- Ae-sun!
- No, no, no.

80
00:04:23,763 --> 00:04:25,556
- That's not what I want.
- Ae-sun!

81
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:28,059
Hey! She's right there.
Right there. Here she is.

82
00:04:28,142 --> 00:04:30,144
- Ae-sun, there you are.
- She'll tell you.

83
00:04:30,228 --> 00:04:31,312
Well?

84
00:04:32,021 --> 00:04:33,690
Wait. Deputy.

85
00:04:35,650 --> 00:04:36,567
Deputy.

86
00:04:50,957 --> 00:04:53,084
She's not gonna start shitting here,
is she?

87
00:04:58,006 --> 00:04:59,007
Hey, get up.

88
00:05:00,633 --> 00:05:02,385
<i>There's an outcry with no sound</i>

89
00:05:03,261 --> 00:05:04,387
What's that?

90
00:05:04,470 --> 00:05:07,265
<i>Lashed by the season's bitter scourge</i>

91
00:05:07,348 --> 00:05:09,809
You're embarrassing yourself.
Stop making a scene.

92
00:05:11,477 --> 00:05:14,188
<i>- If you get fed up with me and--</i>
- Hey, someone get a forklift.

93
00:05:14,272 --> 00:05:15,398
Then run me over!

94
00:05:15,481 --> 00:05:18,151
Hey, this is a gangster.
She's not a high school graduate.

95
00:05:18,234 --> 00:05:21,821
The only gangsters here are the ones
stealing people's livelihoods.

96
00:05:21,904 --> 00:05:23,781
What? You can't be serious!

97
00:05:23,865 --> 00:05:24,824
Bring it on!

98
00:05:24,907 --> 00:05:27,035
Oh, now I'm really getting pissed off!

99
00:05:27,118 --> 00:05:28,411
Bring it on!

100
00:05:28,494 --> 00:05:30,663
Just tell them to pack it up! Come on!

101
00:05:30,747 --> 00:05:32,623
I said, bring it on!

102
00:05:34,459 --> 00:05:36,085
Do your worst!

103
00:05:42,675 --> 00:05:45,553
My goodness,
what happened to the bookworm?

104
00:05:46,137 --> 00:05:47,638
Well, I know what. I know what.

105
00:05:47,722 --> 00:05:49,474
Life happened, that's what.

106
00:05:49,974 --> 00:05:51,225
I don't believe it.

107
00:05:52,810 --> 00:05:53,978
Damn it.

108
00:05:54,062 --> 00:05:55,688
Hey, Bu Sang-gil.

109
00:05:55,772 --> 00:05:56,689
A FRUITFUL FALL

110
00:05:56,773 --> 00:05:58,941
You better compensate us
for the day of lost sales!

111
00:05:59,442 --> 00:06:01,444
OPPOSITION PARTIES FAIL TO AGREE
ON SINGLE CANDIDACY

112
00:06:01,527 --> 00:06:03,363
Politics is as fickle as the wind,
isn't it?

113
00:06:03,988 --> 00:06:07,575
The whole town is talking about
how you could be the next village chief.

114
00:06:07,658 --> 00:06:10,703
Please. I told you.
I have no interest in politics.

115
00:06:10,787 --> 00:06:14,707
That's what you types always say.
Then, lo and behold, you end up running.

116
00:06:15,583 --> 00:06:17,543
This election is between
a government stooge

117
00:06:17,627 --> 00:06:18,753
and real fighters like us.

118
00:06:18,836 --> 00:06:21,172
If we let
that treacherous idiot of a chief

119
00:06:21,255 --> 00:06:23,549
win with all the money
from the Olympic bureaucrats,

120
00:06:23,633 --> 00:06:25,635
then all of us <i>haenyeo </i>are screwed.

121
00:06:25,718 --> 00:06:28,679
If he wants to get called "chief,"
he should be acting like one, right?

122
00:06:28,763 --> 00:06:30,723
I hate how he calls you "deputy"
all the time.

123
00:06:31,349 --> 00:06:33,976
It's all, "Hey, deputy" this,
"deputy" that!

124
00:06:34,060 --> 00:06:34,977
"Hey, deputy!"

125
00:06:35,061 --> 00:06:38,106
- That's how he says it.
- She can't stand being a number two.

126
00:06:38,189 --> 00:06:40,316
If a dog like him can be the chief,
then why not her?

127
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:43,236
Let's make a <i>haenyeo's </i>daughter
village chief.

128
00:06:43,319 --> 00:06:45,905
Will you cut it out?
I have no interest in politics.

129
00:06:45,988 --> 00:06:47,323
I told you that.

130
00:06:47,407 --> 00:06:48,324
Oh?

131
00:06:48,408 --> 00:06:50,576
So we should just ignore

132
00:06:50,660 --> 00:06:51,869
what your husband wants?

133
00:06:53,913 --> 00:06:55,665
Wow, this is a first.

134
00:06:56,666 --> 00:07:00,086
It looks like our captain
is on the campaign trail.

135
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:03,756
All right, you gave us snacks.
Who should we vote for?

136
00:07:04,507 --> 00:07:07,176
We took the bribe, Captain.
Talk to us.

137
00:07:07,844 --> 00:07:08,678
Well,

138
00:07:10,263 --> 00:07:12,265
I don't say this because she's my wife.

139
00:07:12,890 --> 00:07:16,185
She has been a natural leader.
She's been guiding us often.

140
00:07:16,269 --> 00:07:17,478
I witnessed it myself.

141
00:07:19,647 --> 00:07:24,026
More than that, she's smart. In fact,
I've never in my life met anyone smarter.

142
00:07:24,110 --> 00:07:25,194
That's my honest opinion.

143
00:07:25,278 --> 00:07:28,406
Sure, she was smart enough
to make you captain.

144
00:07:35,663 --> 00:07:36,873
Hey.

145
00:07:36,956 --> 00:07:38,708
Let's be frank here.

146
00:07:38,791 --> 00:07:42,003
Are you really okay with
Ae-sun being the village chief?

147
00:07:42,712 --> 00:07:46,507
Your wife would be the first female
village chief Dodong-ri has ever had.

148
00:07:46,591 --> 00:07:48,092
What happens to you?

149
00:07:48,176 --> 00:07:51,387
I'm not sure if that's
respectable for a man.

150
00:07:51,471 --> 00:07:54,182
Sure, she'd be the first, but so would I.

151
00:07:54,265 --> 00:07:56,684
If Ae-sun becomes
the first female chief of the village,

152
00:07:56,767 --> 00:07:59,729
then that would make me
the first husband of the chief.

153
00:08:00,688 --> 00:08:01,689
That's respectable.

154
00:08:01,772 --> 00:08:03,900
I wouldn't even
have to do anything at all.

155
00:08:03,983 --> 00:08:05,985
Well, just slow down, huh?

156
00:08:06,068 --> 00:08:08,279
You're making the rest of us men look bad.

157
00:08:08,362 --> 00:08:11,199
Our captain's dreams
sure sound different from ours.

158
00:08:13,826 --> 00:08:16,454
Here, they just came out with this brand.

159
00:08:20,124 --> 00:08:23,211
<i>All of it. I'm going to be</i>
<i>the chief of the fishing village,</i>

160
00:08:23,294 --> 00:08:26,005
and then I'll be president
five times in a row.

161
00:08:29,300 --> 00:08:30,676
When you grow up, what will you be?

162
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:32,512
What are you asking him for?

163
00:08:32,595 --> 00:08:34,597
- Goodness.
- Oh my.

164
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:36,098
The First Gentleman.

165
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:38,768
The First Gentleman.

166
00:08:39,685 --> 00:08:40,895
Well…

167
00:08:40,978 --> 00:08:42,813
What is it, First Lady?

168
00:08:43,397 --> 00:08:44,315
Those drinks,

169
00:08:45,566 --> 00:08:47,610
there are actually
real, fresh bananas in there.

170
00:08:47,693 --> 00:08:49,320
This is the best quality, you guys.

171
00:08:51,531 --> 00:08:52,490
I see you like it.

172
00:08:55,284 --> 00:08:58,246
It's all right,
but this banana milk is nothing.

173
00:08:58,829 --> 00:09:01,916
<i>That bigwig you're running against</i>
<i>is giving away pork.</i>

174
00:09:01,999 --> 00:09:03,167
<i>Who doesn't love pork?</i>

175
00:09:03,251 --> 00:09:05,836
Listen up.
This isn't just any old pork.

176
00:09:06,420 --> 00:09:08,422
This is Jeju black pork.

177
00:09:08,506 --> 00:09:09,924
Oh yes.

178
00:09:10,007 --> 00:09:11,926
From Jeju Island black pig.

179
00:09:12,009 --> 00:09:14,804
Make sure everyone gets a double serving
of this premium meat.

180
00:09:14,887 --> 00:09:17,348
Premium? This is what we always serve.

181
00:09:17,431 --> 00:09:20,810
Listen up, everybody.
Don't think I have an ulterior motive.

182
00:09:20,893 --> 00:09:24,105
Really, I'm not doing this
for money or honor.

183
00:09:24,647 --> 00:09:26,732
My only concern is, and always has been,

184
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:31,237
"How can I give the folks
in our village something good?"

185
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:33,990
"How can I give folks something to enjoy?"

186
00:09:34,073 --> 00:09:35,491
Can I have some water?

187
00:09:35,575 --> 00:09:37,201
- Garlic, please.
- Water, please.

188
00:09:37,285 --> 00:09:40,830
Could you at least listen to me
when I'm talking to you? Sheesh.

189
00:09:41,330 --> 00:09:43,708
I don't know why
you squeezed us all in here

190
00:09:43,791 --> 00:09:45,585
just to feed us a morsel of pork.

191
00:09:46,627 --> 00:09:49,422
Finish your plate, Grandma.
Then you can order more.

192
00:09:50,298 --> 00:09:52,758
You don't look like one of my supporters,
but here you are.

193
00:09:52,842 --> 00:09:54,927
She's right. You're barely feeding them.

194
00:09:55,011 --> 00:09:57,305
You're frugal, I'll give you that.

195
00:09:57,388 --> 00:09:59,515
So, think about it.

196
00:10:00,141 --> 00:10:03,185
Oh Ae-sun has basically
no history to speak of

197
00:10:03,769 --> 00:10:07,607
whereas my family built this town
and continues to serve!

198
00:10:07,690 --> 00:10:10,943
I ordered soda an hour ago.
When are you gonna serve that?

199
00:10:11,027 --> 00:10:13,195
Not everyone is born a leader,

200
00:10:13,696 --> 00:10:16,449
which is exactly why
we should carefully examine

201
00:10:16,532 --> 00:10:19,410
each candidate's past to check
for any issues or family problems.

202
00:10:19,493 --> 00:10:20,745
What family problems?

203
00:10:20,828 --> 00:10:23,372
I heard Gwan-sik
got an official commendation.

204
00:10:23,873 --> 00:10:26,417
- Do you have any of those?
- It's not a commendation, all right?

205
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:27,710
It's a plaque of appreciation.

206
00:10:27,793 --> 00:10:30,212
I could get a dozen of those things,
no problem.

207
00:10:31,130 --> 00:10:32,506
But you don't have any.

208
00:10:32,590 --> 00:10:34,508
Have you ever saved anyone from drowning?

209
00:10:34,592 --> 00:10:36,927
Stop talking over me! Hush.

210
00:10:37,011 --> 00:10:39,221
You should learn to listen
when someone is talking to you.

211
00:10:39,305 --> 00:10:42,475
All you ladies just want to butt in
the first chance you get, aren't you?

212
00:10:42,558 --> 00:10:45,603
What about you? Why don't you
listen to me about that soda?

213
00:10:46,646 --> 00:10:48,105
Now, as I was saying,

214
00:10:48,189 --> 00:10:51,275
that family isn't exactly
a shining example of behavior.

215
00:10:51,984 --> 00:10:55,321
At 18, they stole high-end jewelry
and ran off together.

216
00:10:55,404 --> 00:10:58,908
- Their daughter was conceived like that.
- She's at Seoul National University.

217
00:10:58,991 --> 00:11:00,618
Well, the second child is a rotten egg!

218
00:11:01,661 --> 00:11:05,414
I don't wanna speak ill
of other people's kids, but him?

219
00:11:06,999 --> 00:11:09,669
- It's hard to say anything good.
- Okay, then don't.

220
00:11:09,752 --> 00:11:11,295
Bring my soda instead.

221
00:11:11,379 --> 00:11:13,547
I'm saying the apple
never falls far from the tree.

222
00:11:13,631 --> 00:11:16,717
When you start with parents like those,
what do you expect to come out?

223
00:11:17,343 --> 00:11:18,719
<i>It's in their genes!</i>

224
00:11:21,597 --> 00:11:25,184
DODONG-RI FISHING CO-OP DEPUTY CHIEF
MOTHER OF YANG EUN-MYEONG

225
00:11:25,267 --> 00:11:26,936
DODONG-RI FISHING CO-OP CHIEF

226
00:11:35,569 --> 00:11:37,738
<i>Did you come here</i>
<i>from the hair salon?</i>

227
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:42,410
Take that off.

228
00:11:44,495 --> 00:11:47,832
So how many other student officers are
bringing their mothers to school today?

229
00:11:50,501 --> 00:11:52,503
I can't believe they made you PE leader.

230
00:11:52,586 --> 00:11:54,630
Of all people.

231
00:11:55,214 --> 00:11:56,632
It's just too funny.

232
00:11:59,301 --> 00:12:00,678
Oh goodness.

233
00:12:00,761 --> 00:12:03,973
I'm sure the other mothers
will have so many questions for me.

234
00:12:04,056 --> 00:12:07,059
Like how your sister made it
into Seoul University.

235
00:12:07,143 --> 00:12:09,478
I'll be they'll wanna know
what our secret was.

236
00:12:09,562 --> 00:12:11,188
About that.

237
00:12:12,815 --> 00:12:14,525
It's at 4:00, right? Let's go.

238
00:12:15,693 --> 00:12:18,237
- Mom.
- Ooh, I hope I'm not too early.

239
00:12:18,904 --> 00:12:21,240
- Mom, wait.
- Is this where all the mothers are?

240
00:12:21,323 --> 00:12:22,700
There are no other mothers.

241
00:12:24,076 --> 00:12:27,288
Why? I thought
this was for all the student officers.

242
00:12:27,913 --> 00:12:30,207
- It's actually just for us.
- What?

243
00:12:33,377 --> 00:12:35,421
Hello, sir. I can't tell you how--

244
00:12:35,504 --> 00:12:36,964
No need to come in, ma'am.

245
00:12:37,047 --> 00:12:38,632
- Follow me outside.
- Huh?

246
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:40,760
To the parking lot?

247
00:12:51,562 --> 00:12:54,023
Apparently, I drive an Onata now!

248
00:12:56,525 --> 00:13:00,112
And another teacher just discovered
he's driving a Hyundai Pon!

249
00:13:00,196 --> 00:13:03,449
The students believe if they get
the initials to their dream colleges,

250
00:13:03,532 --> 00:13:05,576
it will help with their odds
of getting in.

251
00:13:05,659 --> 00:13:07,161
Is that the way your sister did it?

252
00:13:07,745 --> 00:13:10,080
And… and he's not just
stealing these letters.

253
00:13:10,164 --> 00:13:11,540
He's actually selling them off!

254
00:13:13,584 --> 00:13:16,837
Ma'am, I shouldn't have to tell you
how serious this is.

255
00:13:16,921 --> 00:13:18,881
Just look at the principal's car!

256
00:13:19,381 --> 00:13:21,467
Have you ever heard of a Tellar GX?

257
00:13:23,427 --> 00:13:25,805
<i>I've been teaching for more than 20 years.</i>

258
00:13:25,888 --> 00:13:28,224
And in that time,
no student has turned my car

259
00:13:28,307 --> 00:13:30,476
into an Onata until Yang Eun-myeong!

260
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:31,894
I'm sorry, sir.

261
00:13:31,977 --> 00:13:34,230
He only comes to school
for his side hustles.

262
00:13:34,730 --> 00:13:36,357
He's certainly good with his hands.

263
00:13:37,441 --> 00:13:40,820
He's always scheming. Whether it's cutting
a set of ten bus tickets into eleven

264
00:13:40,903 --> 00:13:42,488
for a profit of 50 won

265
00:13:42,571 --> 00:13:44,448
or playing the coin flipping game

266
00:13:44,532 --> 00:13:46,283
and stealing the coin
when no one's looking.

267
00:13:47,284 --> 00:13:49,161
School isn't a business!

268
00:13:49,245 --> 00:13:52,331
It's not a job.
Only the teachers should be getting paid.

269
00:13:53,332 --> 00:13:56,001
He probably makes more money
at this school than I do.

270
00:13:57,253 --> 00:13:58,212
I'm sorry, sir.

271
00:13:58,295 --> 00:14:02,132
You cared so much for your daughter
that you've completely neglected your son.

272
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:05,469
Do you even know what kind of students
he's hanging out with?

273
00:14:19,984 --> 00:14:22,027
That's right, stay away from me.

274
00:14:23,696 --> 00:14:25,114
I don't wanna hear a word.

275
00:14:27,908 --> 00:14:30,703
"All the mothers will be there."
Well, you got me.

276
00:14:31,745 --> 00:14:33,455
What's with these little schemes anyway?

277
00:14:33,956 --> 00:14:35,916
Why can't you just study
like you're supposed to?

278
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:37,918
Why are you so obsessed with money?

279
00:14:38,002 --> 00:14:41,046
You know, I was never embarrassed
at school when your sister was here.

280
00:14:41,130 --> 00:14:43,632
But now I can't look
your teacher in the eye!

281
00:14:44,675 --> 00:14:46,176
Stop hitting the trees!

282
00:14:50,014 --> 00:14:51,515
What's going on with you?

283
00:14:51,599 --> 00:14:52,808
Where did we go wrong?

284
00:14:52,892 --> 00:14:55,394
I said we'd be happy
if you're even half like your sister.

285
00:14:55,477 --> 00:14:57,062
Was that too much to ask?

286
00:14:57,146 --> 00:14:59,189
Right, if I'm not like her,
you can't be chief.

287
00:14:59,273 --> 00:15:01,525
My bad genes are holding you back.

288
00:15:01,609 --> 00:15:04,445
No, that's--
Where did you hear that?

289
00:15:04,528 --> 00:15:07,364
- Bu Sang-gil, that jerk.
- You don't have to lie.

290
00:15:08,407 --> 00:15:10,409
You've always loved her more than me.

291
00:15:33,724 --> 00:15:36,936
<i>The son might be trouble,</i>
<i>but her daughter is a scholar.</i>

292
00:15:37,019 --> 00:15:39,521
<i>Education isn't everything,</i>
<i>is it?</i>

293
00:15:39,605 --> 00:15:42,191
<i>Can education change who her mother is?</i>

294
00:15:42,691 --> 00:15:45,611
<i>Sure, she's at that fancy school…</i>

295
00:15:46,820 --> 00:15:50,324
<i>…but she'll throw it all away</i>
<i>for some boy first chance she gets.</i>

296
00:15:50,407 --> 00:15:52,576
{\an8}CELEBRATING DIRECT PRESIDENTIAL
ELECTION SYSTEM

297
00:15:52,660 --> 00:15:56,789
<i>♪ That my life would change forever… ♪</i>

298
00:15:59,249 --> 00:16:01,919
He's always coming to pick her up.
Is that her boyfriend?

299
00:16:02,002 --> 00:16:03,337
I guess he's well-off.

300
00:16:03,420 --> 00:16:06,423
Even if he is, how can a college student
drive that kind of car?

301
00:16:07,216 --> 00:16:08,801
You know, something's up with her.

302
00:16:09,843 --> 00:16:12,972
I saw it on TV.
Lots of college girls are escorts.

303
00:16:13,639 --> 00:16:16,809
They get paid to go on dates
with older guys and pretend to like them.

304
00:16:17,434 --> 00:16:20,104
Ju-gyeong, listen,
you gotta watch your mouth.

305
00:16:20,187 --> 00:16:23,107
<i>♪ Real fantasy ♪</i>

306
00:16:24,149 --> 00:16:27,611
<i>♪ Illusions are a common thing ♪</i>

307
00:16:27,695 --> 00:16:30,823
<i>♪ I try to live in dreams ♪</i>

308
00:16:30,906 --> 00:16:32,241
<i>♪ It seems as… ♪</i>

309
00:16:32,825 --> 00:16:34,660
He's gotta be from
the US, right?

310
00:16:35,244 --> 00:16:38,539
Look at him. How embarrassing.
He's opening the door and everything.

311
00:16:38,622 --> 00:16:41,333
Does he also slice
pork cutlets for her at restaurants?

312
00:16:42,459 --> 00:16:48,590
<i>♪ A different kind of reality ♪</i>

313
00:16:49,633 --> 00:16:53,470
<i>♪ I dream of loving in the night ♪</i>

314
00:16:53,554 --> 00:16:56,557
<i>♪ And loving seems all right… ♪</i>

315
00:16:57,808 --> 00:16:58,767
Get in.

316
00:16:58,851 --> 00:17:01,353
<i>♪ Fantasy ♪</i>

317
00:17:08,986 --> 00:17:11,071
<i>♪ All you need is love ♪</i>

318
00:17:11,155 --> 00:17:12,740
<i>♪ Ba-ba-da-ba-da ♪</i>

319
00:17:12,823 --> 00:17:14,992
<i>♪ All you need is love ♪</i>

320
00:17:15,075 --> 00:17:17,161
<i>♪ Ba-ba-da-ba-da ♪</i>

321
00:17:18,495 --> 00:17:19,329
Hmm.

322
00:17:20,414 --> 00:17:23,125
You just have to remember
who that girl's parents are,

323
00:17:23,208 --> 00:17:24,835
and the future becomes clear.

324
00:17:24,918 --> 00:17:27,129
I can see it already.

325
00:17:28,088 --> 00:17:31,884
That whole family just has
no… no concept of decency at all.

326
00:17:31,967 --> 00:17:32,968
Don't you think?

327
00:17:33,052 --> 00:17:34,344
Boop!

328
00:17:34,428 --> 00:17:38,557
Fine, so you bought the tree,
but you can't take credit for the rock.

329
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:41,018
You just wrote your name
on public property.

330
00:17:41,101 --> 00:17:42,936
When you get down to it,

331
00:17:43,020 --> 00:17:45,481
Ae-sun doesn't even deserve to be deputy.

332
00:17:45,564 --> 00:17:48,192
Who does she think she is?
She knows nothing at all.

333
00:17:48,275 --> 00:17:51,487
Hey, Captain. Are you actually
running on anything or what?

334
00:17:51,570 --> 00:17:52,404
What?

335
00:17:52,488 --> 00:17:55,157
Because it seems like you're running
just to trash-talk your opponent.

336
00:17:57,409 --> 00:18:00,037
It's not talking trash.

337
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:02,081
It's just discussing morality.

338
00:18:02,164 --> 00:18:05,584
The people have a right to know
who their candidates are, don't they?

339
00:18:05,667 --> 00:18:07,252
{\an8}BADA SEAFOOD HOUSE

340
00:18:07,336 --> 00:18:10,172
I can't believe that scumbag
brought your kids into this.

341
00:18:10,839 --> 00:18:13,967
- It's outrageous.
- Sang-gil crossed the line.

342
00:18:14,718 --> 00:18:16,095
You need to fight back.

343
00:18:17,304 --> 00:18:20,349
<i>If you keep talking like that,</i>
<i>Ae-sun will have to respond.</i>

344
00:18:20,432 --> 00:18:23,268
She's been holding back
because she's got some class.

345
00:18:23,352 --> 00:18:25,479
- But if push comes to shove…
- Oh yes. That's right.

346
00:18:25,562 --> 00:18:28,232
…I imagine she'd have
a thing or two to say about you.

347
00:18:28,732 --> 00:18:32,778
I remember his father
back during the occupation.

348
00:18:33,278 --> 00:18:36,240
He couldn't wait to take on
a Japanese name!

349
00:18:38,700 --> 00:18:40,077
Funny.

350
00:18:40,661 --> 00:18:43,330
But you're not gonna find
any dirt on our side.

351
00:18:43,956 --> 00:18:44,790
After all,

352
00:18:45,582 --> 00:18:48,585
I make contributions to our government,

353
00:18:49,169 --> 00:18:50,796
<i>But Oh Ae-sun, well,</i>

354
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:54,508
<i>I'm pretty sure she's never</i>
<i>given as much as a dime to charity.</i>

355
00:18:56,802 --> 00:18:59,429
Politics is a land
of dog shit anyway.

356
00:18:59,513 --> 00:19:02,641
If you have to roll in it,
better to have black fur than white.

357
00:19:02,724 --> 00:19:05,477
If you roll in crap,
you get dirty all the same.

358
00:19:06,228 --> 00:19:07,104
Black fur or not.

359
00:19:07,187 --> 00:19:09,273
I'll win, but I won't change.

360
00:19:10,357 --> 00:19:13,735
Oh, that's our Oh Ae-sun,
just as proud as ever.

361
00:19:13,819 --> 00:19:16,738
You're not giving out soap.
You're not feeding them pork.

362
00:19:16,822 --> 00:19:18,323
You're not even playing dirty.

363
00:19:19,074 --> 00:19:21,285
Well, you might just lose. You might lose.

364
00:19:22,202 --> 00:19:24,371
Ae-sun, it's only fair.

365
00:19:24,454 --> 00:19:27,624
The villagers have a right to know
exactly who Sang-gil is.

366
00:19:27,708 --> 00:19:30,210
And he already crossed the line
to attack you.

367
00:19:30,294 --> 00:19:32,462
You may as well get him back too!

368
00:19:32,546 --> 00:19:36,967
Hey, a caterpillar will get eaten
if it stays in its cocoon too long.

369
00:19:37,050 --> 00:19:40,387
If that caterpillar struggles
and breaks out of its shell,

370
00:19:40,470 --> 00:19:42,139
it flies away a butterfly.

371
00:19:42,222 --> 00:19:45,976
You need to jump over the hurdle
before you fight your way out, Ae-sun.

372
00:19:46,727 --> 00:19:50,981
♪ <i>Clock strikes upon the hour</i>
<i>And the sun begins to fade </i>♪

373
00:19:51,064 --> 00:19:53,525
<i>♪ Still enough time to figure out ♪</i>

374
00:19:53,609 --> 00:19:56,737
<i>♪ How to chase Ae-sun away ♪</i>

375
00:19:56,820 --> 00:19:58,989
<i>♪ She's done all right up till now ♪</i>

376
00:20:00,073 --> 00:20:02,951
<i>♪ But I'll win reelection anyhow ♪</i>

377
00:20:03,035 --> 00:20:05,287
<i>♪ And when the night falls upon us ♪</i>

378
00:20:05,829 --> 00:20:07,331
<i>♪ Bu Sang-gil calls ♪</i>

379
00:20:07,414 --> 00:20:08,999
<i>♪ Da, da, da, da! ♪</i>

380
00:20:09,082 --> 00:20:11,335
<i>♪ Oh, if you wanna vote for me ♪</i>

381
00:20:11,418 --> 00:20:13,795
<i>♪ You can't find any dirt ♪</i>

382
00:20:13,879 --> 00:20:15,047
Stop it, jeez!

383
00:20:15,130 --> 00:20:17,549
I'm not voting for someone
who ruins my appetite!

384
00:20:20,177 --> 00:20:21,511
Are those noodles coming?

385
00:20:21,595 --> 00:20:23,263
Mr. Gu, I think you'd sing better.

386
00:20:23,347 --> 00:20:25,724
He's always on his wife's case, isn't he?

387
00:20:27,976 --> 00:20:30,604
What's taking you so long
to cook those noodles?

388
00:20:31,897 --> 00:20:33,315
You're walking home tonight.

389
00:20:33,815 --> 00:20:35,651
You're not allowed in my car, understand?

390
00:20:35,734 --> 00:20:37,069
Hey, Bu Sang-gil,

391
00:20:37,694 --> 00:20:40,155
isn't it a bit ironic
your last name means "deputy?"

392
00:20:40,239 --> 00:20:42,824
Maybe you should just accept
that no matter where you go,

393
00:20:42,908 --> 00:20:44,743
you'll always be second fiddle.

394
00:20:47,996 --> 00:20:50,040
- What?
- Are you even voting for me?

395
00:20:50,123 --> 00:20:52,417
Or did you just come here
to make trouble or what?

396
00:20:52,501 --> 00:20:54,002
Is this 'cause I didn't get you a soda?

397
00:20:54,086 --> 00:20:57,130
Hey, if you do end up losing,
here's some advice.

398
00:20:57,214 --> 00:20:58,382
Why would I lose?

399
00:20:58,465 --> 00:21:01,843
Do you have any idea how much I've spent
on pork and noodles already, hmm?

400
00:21:01,927 --> 00:21:04,388
Don't settle for anything less
than deputy chief.

401
00:21:04,471 --> 00:21:06,348
It's like when you're watching <i>Jeopardy,</i>

402
00:21:06,431 --> 00:21:08,767
and someone gets out ahead
only to finish last.

403
00:21:09,268 --> 00:21:11,645
There's nothing more pathetic, is there?

404
00:21:11,728 --> 00:21:13,939
Spare yourself and finish second at least.

405
00:21:14,439 --> 00:21:15,565
- Hey!
- "Hey"?

406
00:21:15,649 --> 00:21:17,651
Did you just "hey" me?

407
00:21:17,734 --> 00:21:19,444
Where the hell are those noodles?

408
00:21:21,613 --> 00:21:23,615
You can vote for Oh Ae-sun if you want.

409
00:21:24,992 --> 00:21:26,576
FROM BU SANG-GIL, CANDIDATE 1

410
00:21:26,660 --> 00:21:30,247
But no matter how smart the Oh family is
or how undeserving the Bu family may be,

411
00:21:30,998 --> 00:21:33,875
there's no woman chief anywhere in Korea.

412
00:21:33,959 --> 00:21:36,628
- No, of course not.
- Wow. A box of cigarettes each?

413
00:21:36,712 --> 00:21:39,464
There's more?
I wish every day was election day.

414
00:21:40,882 --> 00:21:43,468
Who can stand in the way of a typhoon?

415
00:21:43,969 --> 00:21:46,555
Democracy is just data.

416
00:21:47,055 --> 00:21:48,682
That's how it goes.

417
00:21:49,850 --> 00:21:51,351
I vote Bu Sang-gil!

418
00:21:51,435 --> 00:21:54,146
- I'll drink to that! Drink!
- Raise a glass.

419
00:21:54,229 --> 00:21:56,023
Here, pour me some.

420
00:21:56,940 --> 00:21:58,525
Yeah, that's it.

421
00:21:59,192 --> 00:22:01,570
- Who's your chief?
- Mr. Bu!

422
00:22:01,653 --> 00:22:04,364
- Who's your chief?
- Mr. Bu!

423
00:22:04,448 --> 00:22:07,367
- Who is your chief?
- Mr. Bu!

424
00:22:10,954 --> 00:22:14,333
Lucky you.
I hope you're the chief till you die.

425
00:22:14,916 --> 00:22:18,754
What can I say?
Indecency seems to run in the Oh family.

426
00:22:18,837 --> 00:22:20,714
Just have a look at my own daughters.

427
00:22:20,797 --> 00:22:22,883
Hyeon-suk, which stands for
"wise" and "enlightened,"

428
00:22:22,966 --> 00:22:23,925
and Jeong-suk,

429
00:22:24,843 --> 00:22:26,970
which stands for "silent."

430
00:22:27,054 --> 00:22:29,890
Oh, he's a damn fool
if there ever was one.

431
00:22:37,522 --> 00:22:38,440
I have…

432
00:22:39,983 --> 00:22:43,653
I have absolutely nothing
in my past to be ashamed of, Mi-suk.

433
00:22:45,113 --> 00:22:47,199
Life's a bitch, huh?

434
00:22:47,282 --> 00:22:51,036
It's always so difficult
to get anything done.

435
00:22:51,703 --> 00:22:53,914
You can sell everything
in the display case

436
00:22:53,997 --> 00:22:55,791
and still wind up with nothing.

437
00:22:58,168 --> 00:23:02,172
There's hardly any money to be made from
a real estate office on a tiny island.

438
00:23:02,255 --> 00:23:06,551
I thought that helping out
the Olympics Committee was my big break,

439
00:23:07,135 --> 00:23:09,763
but those <i>haenyeo </i>are so stubborn.

440
00:23:10,889 --> 00:23:12,057
You know what I'm like.

441
00:23:12,140 --> 00:23:14,309
- Mm.
- I'm a softie.

442
00:23:14,893 --> 00:23:18,021
Mi-suk, I swear… I'll take care of it.

443
00:23:18,939 --> 00:23:20,607
I'm your guy.

444
00:23:21,149 --> 00:23:24,319
I'm practically a shoo-in
for reelection now.

445
00:23:25,612 --> 00:23:26,488
Really?

446
00:23:26,571 --> 00:23:29,324
You'd take care of everything
just like that?

447
00:23:29,408 --> 00:23:31,785
I wouldn't even have to pay
a fee or anything, Bu Sang-gil?

448
00:23:31,868 --> 00:23:32,911
30%.

449
00:23:33,787 --> 00:23:34,621
What?

450
00:23:34,704 --> 00:23:35,789
30/70 split.

451
00:23:38,375 --> 00:23:40,836
Oh, all right.

452
00:23:40,919 --> 00:23:43,713
After all,
cooperation makes the world go round.

453
00:23:43,797 --> 00:23:45,966
Mi-suk, I'm your guy.

454
00:23:46,675 --> 00:23:49,177
Dodong-ri's own Bu Sang-gil.

455
00:23:49,886 --> 00:23:50,762
Mi-suk.

456
00:23:52,013 --> 00:23:53,265
Listen.

457
00:23:53,348 --> 00:23:57,519
I may have money, but I don't have
enough romance in my life.

458
00:23:58,687 --> 00:24:00,856
I'm really quite a lonely guy.

459
00:24:05,068 --> 00:24:06,653
You don't have to be shy.

460
00:24:09,197 --> 00:24:10,991
Oh, I'm not.

461
00:24:12,159 --> 00:24:13,869
Come on.

462
00:24:14,744 --> 00:24:18,707
You don't think I'm offering
to help you for the money, do you?

463
00:24:19,791 --> 00:24:23,253
Well, if it's not for the money,
then what's it for?

464
00:24:26,465 --> 00:24:27,799
Don't make that face.

465
00:24:29,759 --> 00:24:30,844
What face?

466
00:24:32,846 --> 00:24:35,348
It's the Olympics, after all.

467
00:24:35,432 --> 00:24:38,268
Walls are falling down all over the world,

468
00:24:38,351 --> 00:24:40,770
even in the Soviet Union.

469
00:24:41,313 --> 00:24:43,273
We could just break down the wall

470
00:24:44,774 --> 00:24:46,151
in between us two.

471
00:24:51,865 --> 00:24:53,950
Stop drinking.
You'll ruin your liver.

472
00:24:54,993 --> 00:24:55,827
Oh.

473
00:24:56,411 --> 00:25:00,248
But the quickest way to a man's heart
is through his stomach.

474
00:25:04,377 --> 00:25:07,047
Perhaps this isn't just a piece of fish

475
00:25:07,130 --> 00:25:10,634
but a trap for my stomach,
and my heart has taken the bait.

476
00:25:11,343 --> 00:25:12,677
Maybe.

477
00:25:13,595 --> 00:25:14,429
Oh, thank you.

478
00:25:15,180 --> 00:25:19,392
These abalones are helping my heart
come out of its shell.

479
00:25:23,396 --> 00:25:25,148
Shut up and eat your shrimp.

480
00:25:26,858 --> 00:25:30,946
Your shrimp is really sending
the blood rushing to my… "muscle."

481
00:25:31,029 --> 00:25:32,739
You're so dirty!

482
00:25:32,822 --> 00:25:35,033
Wait, wait, I'm talking about…
It's my heart.

483
00:25:36,117 --> 00:25:38,370
I mean my heart.
The blood's rushing to my heart.

484
00:25:39,204 --> 00:25:41,414
Oh my God, you're such a clown.

485
00:25:41,498 --> 00:25:42,958
Oh! You're awful!

486
00:25:48,046 --> 00:25:49,172
Hey, listen.

487
00:25:51,299 --> 00:25:52,884
I thought this was just dinner.

488
00:25:54,803 --> 00:25:57,055
Why are you tormenting my lonely heart?

489
00:25:57,138 --> 00:25:59,099
Huh?

490
00:26:00,684 --> 00:26:03,478
- You're a naughty girl, aren't you?
- That tickles.

491
00:26:04,938 --> 00:26:06,481
Disgusting.

492
00:26:06,565 --> 00:26:09,276
Is this how you think
a village chief should act?

493
00:26:10,694 --> 00:26:14,281
You need to jump over the hurdle
before you fight your way out, Ae-sun.

494
00:26:16,324 --> 00:26:17,450
Oh my.

495
00:26:17,534 --> 00:26:19,744
Wait, where are you going?

496
00:26:20,412 --> 00:26:22,956
Damn it, what the hell
did you come in here for?

497
00:26:24,249 --> 00:26:27,586
Well, well, well, if it isn't
"Mr. Snitch-for-the-government."

498
00:26:27,669 --> 00:26:31,006
God, <i>meongge </i>guts are less gross than you.

499
00:26:31,631 --> 00:26:33,800
Who the hell are you
to judge me?

500
00:26:33,883 --> 00:26:38,138
What I do in private
is none of your goddamn business!

501
00:26:38,221 --> 00:26:41,683
Well, we work here. Remember? Moron.

502
00:26:41,766 --> 00:26:44,811
While you were telling that woman
the quickest way to a man's heart,

503
00:26:44,894 --> 00:26:47,022
she was cracking
your wallet open like <i>meongge.</i>

504
00:26:48,523 --> 00:26:50,483
Why were you
eavesdropping on us?

505
00:26:50,984 --> 00:26:52,777
- Why?
- I just realized.

506
00:26:53,278 --> 00:26:54,904
You're only village chief

507
00:26:54,988 --> 00:26:57,407
so you can massage
the feet of another man's wife!

508
00:26:59,159 --> 00:27:00,577
How dare you speak to me like that!

509
00:27:01,411 --> 00:27:04,247
Whatever your reasons,
you sure can't be chief anymore.

510
00:27:09,753 --> 00:27:12,213
Why can't I be chief though? Tell me.

511
00:27:12,297 --> 00:27:14,049
You're like a stray dog who goes around

512
00:27:14,132 --> 00:27:16,885
sticking his nose
into everyone's business.

513
00:27:16,968 --> 00:27:19,638
Are you really surprised eventually
people would get fed up with you?

514
00:27:19,721 --> 00:27:24,643
Yeah, we wouldn't even feed rotten rice
to a mutt like you, Sang-gil.

515
00:27:24,726 --> 00:27:28,313
But you want us to make you chief?
We have had it with your crap!

516
00:27:31,232 --> 00:27:32,984
How dare you. Really?

517
00:27:34,069 --> 00:27:36,863
You don't even… you don't even know!

518
00:27:36,946 --> 00:27:39,407
You don't have a clue
what really happened.

519
00:27:40,033 --> 00:27:43,161
All she said was that
her feet were asleep, okay?

520
00:27:43,244 --> 00:27:46,331
Yeah, right.
While your poor wife is aching all over.

521
00:27:46,956 --> 00:27:48,124
Some role model.

522
00:27:48,208 --> 00:27:50,960
Dragging Ae-sun's family into the race.

523
00:27:51,044 --> 00:27:53,254
So her son is a bit of a troublemaker.

524
00:27:53,338 --> 00:27:54,798
Does that make her one too?

525
00:27:55,674 --> 00:27:57,550
My son is smart in his own way.

526
00:27:57,634 --> 00:27:59,511
So what? What now, Ae-sun?

527
00:27:59,594 --> 00:28:01,680
What'll you do? Are you gonna tell on me?

528
00:28:02,555 --> 00:28:05,266
Naturally, naturally,
we will tell everyone and rat you out.

529
00:28:05,350 --> 00:28:07,560
We'll tell everyone,
and Ae-sun will be chief.

530
00:28:07,644 --> 00:28:08,645
That's right.

531
00:28:08,728 --> 00:28:09,896
Is that a fact?

532
00:28:10,563 --> 00:28:12,065
Is that the way you wanna win?

533
00:28:13,149 --> 00:28:14,275
People have a right

534
00:28:15,360 --> 00:28:16,319
to know who we are.

535
00:28:16,986 --> 00:28:20,949
It's not talking trash.
It's just discussing morality.

536
00:28:21,533 --> 00:28:23,702
Everyone has the right to know
their candidates, right?

537
00:28:23,785 --> 00:28:25,453
That's what you said, isn't it?

538
00:28:25,537 --> 00:28:28,206
- Oh, Ae-sun!
- Oh.

539
00:28:30,041 --> 00:28:32,127
You little…

540
00:28:37,716 --> 00:28:39,300
You shouldn't have.

541
00:28:39,384 --> 00:28:40,802
THE 7TH DODONG-RI CHIEF, OH AE-SUN

542
00:28:40,885 --> 00:28:42,011
Oh my!

543
00:28:42,095 --> 00:28:46,808
Ae-sun! Oh Ae-sun!
Oh Ae-sun! Oh Ae-sun!

544
00:28:46,891 --> 00:28:48,935
<i>Ae-sun gave it</i>
<i>her best shot once again.</i>

545
00:28:49,018 --> 00:28:50,353
Oh, look!

546
00:28:50,895 --> 00:28:52,814
Wow, the school lent this to us?

547
00:28:52,897 --> 00:28:55,233
They only use it
for sports day once a year.

548
00:28:55,316 --> 00:28:56,151
Wow.

549
00:28:56,234 --> 00:28:58,528
<i>She hit the bull's-eye</i>
<i>right in the middle.</i>

550
00:28:59,028 --> 00:29:01,072
- <i>That day, Jeju Island…</i>
- Chief!

551
00:29:01,156 --> 00:29:03,783
<i>- …got its first-ever female village chief.</i>
- Hey, Chief.

552
00:29:03,867 --> 00:29:05,493
Chief! Oh, hey!

553
00:29:05,577 --> 00:29:06,661
Uh, yes?

554
00:29:06,745 --> 00:29:09,122
- Look, the rice cake is here.
- Oh, bring it out.

555
00:29:09,748 --> 00:29:13,209
- Chief Oh, we're out of <i>makgeolli.</i>
- Oh, really?

556
00:29:14,210 --> 00:29:16,504
Chief Oh, any more blankets?

557
00:29:16,588 --> 00:29:17,797
- Uh-huh!
- Chief!

558
00:29:18,548 --> 00:29:22,177
It's the school asking if you can return
the banner by sports day, if that's okay?

559
00:29:23,678 --> 00:29:25,889
<i>It pulled</i>
<i>at her heartstrings.</i>

560
00:29:30,101 --> 00:29:33,813
<i>Many years later, when</i>
<i>Mom joined Lim Young-woong's fan club,</i>

561
00:29:33,897 --> 00:29:36,691
<i>her username was Chief Oh.</i>

562
00:29:39,819 --> 00:29:40,695
Hey, Chief Oh!

563
00:29:41,780 --> 00:29:44,407
Come over here and have a taste of this!
You have first dibs!

564
00:29:44,991 --> 00:29:45,867
Okay.

565
00:29:46,826 --> 00:29:48,036
Okay!

566
00:29:57,629 --> 00:29:59,672
- These are ready.
- Okay.

567
00:30:05,220 --> 00:30:07,180
There she is!

568
00:30:07,263 --> 00:30:09,057
{\an8}THE 5TH AND 6TH FISHING CO-OP CHIEF
BU SANG-GIL

569
00:30:09,140 --> 00:30:11,768
{\an8}Here, eat, eat, eat, eat.
I made so much.

570
00:30:19,108 --> 00:30:20,360
One more time!

571
00:30:22,946 --> 00:30:24,572
You serving meat at this thing?

572
00:30:25,281 --> 00:30:26,908
Or are you too goddamn cheap?

573
00:30:26,991 --> 00:30:30,829
Goodness. What's the point
of sitting here all angry?

574
00:30:30,912 --> 00:30:33,623
Why would I miss
my successor's inauguration ceremony?

575
00:30:33,706 --> 00:30:35,792
She doesn't know anything
about being chief.

576
00:30:35,875 --> 00:30:37,585
She needs all the advice she can get.

577
00:30:37,669 --> 00:30:41,589
Well, if you weren't here,
you'd seem a small man indeed.

578
00:30:41,673 --> 00:30:44,050
For your information, I have resigned.

579
00:30:44,551 --> 00:30:46,177
I stepped down on my own accord.

580
00:30:47,178 --> 00:30:50,849
You know the 80-year-old grandpa
who runs the convenience store?

581
00:30:52,225 --> 00:30:55,186
He's never said more than
two words to me before,

582
00:30:55,270 --> 00:30:59,315
but the other day, he asked if I knew
about Sang-gil and the foot massage.

583
00:31:00,024 --> 00:31:04,529
Oh, come on. How many times
do I have to say her feet were asleep?

584
00:31:05,530 --> 00:31:07,699
I would have done the same for anyone.

585
00:31:20,420 --> 00:31:23,506
I'll be serving
my daughter-in-law the rest of my life.

586
00:31:24,048 --> 00:31:27,343
Everyone in the family
is a bigwig politician now.

587
00:31:27,427 --> 00:31:30,305
If Ae-sun is the chief,
her husband's the consort,

588
00:31:30,805 --> 00:31:32,765
and I'm sort of like the queen mother.

589
00:31:32,849 --> 00:31:36,102
Jeez. So, yet again,
she is completely lost in her delusions.

590
00:31:36,185 --> 00:31:38,813
Isn't she something else?
Ever since she met Gwan-sik,

591
00:31:38,897 --> 00:31:40,189
things turned around for her.

592
00:31:40,273 --> 00:31:43,192
I can't tell if you're showing off or not.

593
00:31:43,276 --> 00:31:44,777
Showing off?

594
00:31:45,278 --> 00:31:47,155
How's your daughter-in-law?

595
00:31:47,238 --> 00:31:48,364
Still a gambler, no?

596
00:31:48,948 --> 00:31:50,241
Gambler?

597
00:31:50,325 --> 00:31:52,201
Hurry! We're out of <i>pajeon!</i>

598
00:31:52,285 --> 00:31:55,371
- Jeez.
- The First Gentleman is super busy.

599
00:31:55,455 --> 00:31:57,081
Don't call him First Gentleman.

600
00:31:58,750 --> 00:32:01,294
Good lord, son,
do you have to wear that apron?

601
00:32:01,377 --> 00:32:02,754
- Hey, Ma?
- What?

602
00:32:02,837 --> 00:32:04,964
Can you make them a little bigger? Please?

603
00:32:05,048 --> 00:32:07,175
Why, that…

604
00:32:08,801 --> 00:32:10,470
Now he's pissing me off.

605
00:32:12,221 --> 00:32:15,558
I think I understand.
You're happy Ae-sun is the chief,

606
00:32:15,642 --> 00:32:17,352
but you're also not.

607
00:32:17,435 --> 00:32:18,770
What's so funny?

608
00:32:19,562 --> 00:32:22,398
I've never seen you before. You know me?

609
00:32:22,482 --> 00:32:24,067
Yes, Chief Oh is on it!

610
00:32:24,150 --> 00:32:25,485
I'll be right there!

611
00:32:30,114 --> 00:32:32,367
- Oh my goodness!
- Now what's wrong?

612
00:32:32,867 --> 00:32:35,161
Like you never saw
your mother-in-law at work?

613
00:32:35,244 --> 00:32:38,373
Is this revenge?
Your way of getting back at me?

614
00:32:38,873 --> 00:32:41,084
Please, I'm not talking about that.

615
00:32:41,167 --> 00:32:42,001
Sure.

616
00:32:42,085 --> 00:32:45,254
Why are you making
my opponent's wife make our <i>jeon?</i>

617
00:32:49,801 --> 00:32:51,719
It's unbelievable, but true!

618
00:32:51,803 --> 00:32:53,846
Bu Sang-gil massaged her feet!

619
00:32:57,266 --> 00:33:00,937
Don't listen to them.
You know how an election can get.

620
00:33:01,854 --> 00:33:04,482
Everyone shares all the negative stories
they can think of,

621
00:33:05,066 --> 00:33:07,610
even about your great-great-grandfather.

622
00:33:08,111 --> 00:33:10,446
You should've told them
that I went dancing back then.

623
00:33:10,530 --> 00:33:12,323
No one ever found that out.

624
00:33:14,617 --> 00:33:15,785
I'm very sorry.

625
00:33:15,868 --> 00:33:20,289
I feel like I insulted you
discussing your sensitive issues.

626
00:33:21,207 --> 00:33:23,710
By the way, just between you and me,

627
00:33:24,627 --> 00:33:27,088
we took care of
the real estate lady on our end.

628
00:33:27,630 --> 00:33:29,257
I don't care about her.

629
00:33:29,340 --> 00:33:32,969
Gyeong-suk from the salon.
Mi-suk from the real estate office.

630
00:33:33,469 --> 00:33:34,971
Well, for such a tiny island,

631
00:33:35,054 --> 00:33:38,141
there are so many women
with such a bad taste in men.

632
00:33:39,225 --> 00:33:40,268
However,

633
00:33:41,144 --> 00:33:44,564
it's true that I'm the worst of them all.

634
00:33:48,234 --> 00:33:50,361
Listen, why don't you go home?

635
00:33:50,445 --> 00:33:53,197
People want to gossip.
You know, that's all.

636
00:33:53,281 --> 00:33:55,575
You think they're saying
I have no self-respect?

637
00:33:56,617 --> 00:34:02,373
No, I only meant that I feel awful
seeing you make <i>jeon </i>for our party.

638
00:34:02,457 --> 00:34:05,251
I want to, though,
because it's my prerogative.

639
00:34:05,960 --> 00:34:07,670
I have every right to be here.

640
00:34:09,714 --> 00:34:11,049
Besides, I voted for you.

641
00:34:12,967 --> 00:34:15,970
So, at the very least,
I think I deserve a drink

642
00:34:16,054 --> 00:34:17,722
that you pour me yourself.

643
00:34:21,392 --> 00:34:23,186
Yeong-ran, listen.

644
00:34:23,770 --> 00:34:27,356
When you go home,
no, until the day you die,

645
00:34:27,440 --> 00:34:30,234
tell your husband you voted for him, hmm?

646
00:34:31,736 --> 00:34:35,406
<i>Hey, Yeong-ran,</i>
<i>who did you vote for?</i>

647
00:34:45,416 --> 00:34:47,085
Why can't you answer me?

648
00:34:47,668 --> 00:34:48,920
You didn't vote for me.

649
00:34:49,003 --> 00:34:51,547
Come on, now.
What are you picking on Mom for?

650
00:34:51,631 --> 00:34:53,341
Hey, you little brat.

651
00:34:53,424 --> 00:34:55,468
Don't you disrespect me. What do you know?

652
00:34:56,177 --> 00:34:58,387
You don't know jack shit about anything.

653
00:35:03,101 --> 00:35:07,188
Why? Why? Tell me why.

654
00:35:07,271 --> 00:35:09,690
Why did the governor come today?

655
00:35:09,774 --> 00:35:13,236
Why would the governor come
to a village chief's inauguration?

656
00:35:13,319 --> 00:35:14,779
He didn't come to mine!

657
00:35:14,862 --> 00:35:16,114
The governor?

658
00:35:16,197 --> 00:35:18,366
Gwan-sik got a plaque of honor.

659
00:35:19,033 --> 00:35:20,868
That's why the governor attended.

660
00:35:20,952 --> 00:35:22,662
For jumping into the water?

661
00:35:23,287 --> 00:35:26,499
If I saw someone drowning,
I would jump in a hundred times.

662
00:35:27,083 --> 00:35:29,210
I'd get a hundred commendations!

663
00:35:29,293 --> 00:35:33,756
Wow. I heard there was a reward,
that they're getting a trip and stuff.

664
00:35:34,465 --> 00:35:35,424
That's right.

665
00:35:36,259 --> 00:35:38,052
The governor likes Gwan-sik.

666
00:35:39,011 --> 00:35:40,304
He really does.

667
00:35:42,557 --> 00:35:43,933
Of course he does.

668
00:35:45,643 --> 00:35:47,103
Of course he does.

669
00:35:47,186 --> 00:35:49,313
Why? Why?

670
00:35:50,273 --> 00:35:55,069
Why does everyone here just love
that little stupid punk? Why?

671
00:35:55,153 --> 00:35:57,655
GOVERNOR HWANG IN-SU
CONGRATULATIONS ON YOUR INAUGURATION

672
00:36:01,450 --> 00:36:04,912
If your grandma were alive,
she would've drowned her in red beans.

673
00:36:17,842 --> 00:36:20,011
Come on, let's dance the night away!

674
00:36:22,805 --> 00:36:26,475
My God. What's going on over here?
Come on!

675
00:36:26,976 --> 00:36:29,812
You ought to be ashamed of yourself!
We're going home!

676
00:36:35,985 --> 00:36:38,362
Dad, you have to stop her. She's so drunk!

677
00:36:42,700 --> 00:36:46,204
Goodness. She loves Busan, doesn't she?

678
00:36:46,954 --> 00:36:48,623
She calls herself a bookworm.

679
00:36:48,706 --> 00:36:51,500
You're no bookworm! Just a lousy dancer!

680
00:36:59,383 --> 00:37:01,093
Do you see
what she's doing with that pole?

681
00:37:01,177 --> 00:37:03,930
Go throw those red beans at her.

682
00:37:12,188 --> 00:37:13,189
Dad!

683
00:37:13,272 --> 00:37:15,608
Leave her alone.
Let her have her fun, kid.

684
00:37:17,151 --> 00:37:19,820
I'm so glad I have a dog.

685
00:37:19,904 --> 00:37:21,906
Oh, where is he?

686
00:37:22,782 --> 00:37:24,408
Let's go, Duraengi.

687
00:37:24,492 --> 00:37:26,452
Here, Duraengi. Here, boy.

688
00:37:27,286 --> 00:37:28,537
Let's go, honey.

689
00:37:29,288 --> 00:37:30,414
That's a good boy.

690
00:37:42,134 --> 00:37:42,969
Hey, Dad.

691
00:37:43,678 --> 00:37:44,887
I can take her.

692
00:37:45,471 --> 00:37:46,305
You happy?

693
00:37:47,932 --> 00:37:48,891
Yeah.

694
00:37:49,558 --> 00:37:50,643
I am.

695
00:37:51,644 --> 00:37:54,647
I'm <i>so </i>happy.

696
00:37:56,315 --> 00:37:59,694
You're not a vice president,
a deputy director, or a deputy chief.

697
00:38:00,486 --> 00:38:01,821
You're chief, period.

698
00:38:04,365 --> 00:38:06,367
You know, it's strange.

699
00:38:06,450 --> 00:38:10,663
Even though I've finally lost the "deputy"
from my title after 30 years,

700
00:38:12,206 --> 00:38:15,042
the person I wanna tell the most
isn't here.

701
00:38:20,715 --> 00:38:25,428
I wouldn't say I wanna go back
to my childhood, because it was horrible,

702
00:38:26,846 --> 00:38:29,473
but if there were any way I could go back,

703
00:38:32,059 --> 00:38:33,477
I think I would.

704
00:38:35,271 --> 00:38:39,442
<i>If only for the chance</i>
<i>to hold my mother's hand one more time.</i>

705
00:38:40,568 --> 00:38:43,571
Do you know the reason
why I became the vice president now?

706
00:38:44,363 --> 00:38:46,532
It's so that I can be chief in the future.

707
00:38:46,615 --> 00:38:48,451
It's like diving.

708
00:38:48,534 --> 00:38:50,911
You start in the shallow water,
then go deeper.

709
00:38:52,747 --> 00:38:55,708
Little by little, I'll build experience
and become chief one day.

710
00:38:55,791 --> 00:38:58,627
There's no one on the island
more powerful than a chief.

711
00:38:59,670 --> 00:39:02,840
Even Auntie Gyeong-ja never forgets
to pay her loans back.

712
00:39:02,923 --> 00:39:07,178
Okay, one day, you'll be chief
so I can be the chief's mother.

713
00:39:07,762 --> 00:39:09,764
Will you make rice cake when it happens?

714
00:39:10,556 --> 00:39:14,268
I'm going to make so much rice cake,
it'll pile up as high as a mountain.

715
00:39:14,352 --> 00:39:17,229
- You'd be happy?
- Uh-huh. I'd be happy.

716
00:39:17,313 --> 00:39:18,397
Very much so.

717
00:39:20,441 --> 00:39:21,734
Actually, I'm holding back.

718
00:39:22,401 --> 00:39:25,571
I'm saving up all my happiness
for when that day comes.

719
00:39:28,449 --> 00:39:30,910
Go on, take as much as you want.

720
00:39:30,993 --> 00:39:34,455
I want everyone to know how happy I am.
I'm not holding back.

721
00:39:36,665 --> 00:39:38,334
- Ooh!
- Go on.

722
00:39:38,417 --> 00:39:41,837
- Double portions for everyone.
- Oh, goodness, look.

723
00:39:42,463 --> 00:39:43,422
Oh my.

724
00:39:45,257 --> 00:39:48,302
With these nets,
you supported me when my mom couldn't.

725
00:39:48,886 --> 00:39:51,180
Now she needs you
to brag about me for her.

726
00:39:51,263 --> 00:39:53,432
- Oh my.
- Oh, goodness.

727
00:39:53,516 --> 00:39:57,478
You must've had a lot of rice.
Why did you make so much?

728
00:39:58,062 --> 00:39:59,730
This is Gwang-rye's doing.

729
00:39:59,814 --> 00:40:01,816
Thank you, Gwang-rye, for the rice!

730
00:40:02,316 --> 00:40:03,526
Oh my.

731
00:40:04,360 --> 00:40:05,194
Gwang-rye.

732
00:40:05,820 --> 00:40:10,157
If you could only see your daughter now.
Grown-up and the village chief.

733
00:40:11,158 --> 00:40:13,202
Remember when she was ten years old?

734
00:40:13,828 --> 00:40:16,414
I can still see her wearing
her funeral dress.

735
00:40:16,997 --> 00:40:18,332
Poor dear.

736
00:40:18,416 --> 00:40:20,709
I wondered if she'd make it.

737
00:40:20,793 --> 00:40:24,088
Who knew that not only
would she make it, but she would thrive?

738
00:40:24,171 --> 00:40:27,383
If Gwang-rye were with us,
she'd drum and play

739
00:40:27,466 --> 00:40:29,885
all around Mount Hallasan with us today.

740
00:40:29,969 --> 00:40:33,180
You had to dig out the frozen ground
with your tiny, little hand

741
00:40:33,264 --> 00:40:34,974
and bury your heart in it.

742
00:40:35,057 --> 00:40:37,268
Your harvesting season has come at last.

743
00:40:39,228 --> 00:40:42,148
Gwang-rye's persimmon tree
is growing well, isn't it?

744
00:40:42,648 --> 00:40:44,817
Growing tall and strong.

745
00:40:44,900 --> 00:40:48,112
<i>It was now fall,</i>
<i>the season of harvest,</i>

746
00:40:49,071 --> 00:40:53,033
<i>when all kinds of fruits</i>
<i>were ripening on the vine.</i>

747
00:41:06,297 --> 00:41:09,592
<i>Their harvest was beginning</i>
<i>to overflow the basket.</i>

748
00:41:11,719 --> 00:41:16,307
<i>But depending on where we were,</i>
<i>the sun bathed us in a different light.</i>

749
00:41:23,522 --> 00:41:25,566
Oh, look.

750
00:41:34,867 --> 00:41:35,868
Why, uh…

751
00:41:36,952 --> 00:41:39,413
- Huh?
- Why are you still in the front seat?

752
00:41:39,497 --> 00:41:40,539
Oh.

753
00:41:41,582 --> 00:41:42,625
You know,

754
00:41:44,335 --> 00:41:45,794
it's fun sometimes.

755
00:41:48,589 --> 00:41:49,673
Thanks again.

756
00:41:51,467 --> 00:41:53,260
She can't stand seeing me in here.

757
00:41:53,344 --> 00:41:55,054
Oh, that mean girl you told me about?

758
00:41:55,137 --> 00:41:55,971
Yeah.

759
00:41:56,055 --> 00:41:56,889
Yeong-beom!

760
00:42:02,645 --> 00:42:03,562
Yeong-beom!

761
00:42:16,408 --> 00:42:18,661
Let me know
if you would like anything else, okay?

762
00:42:20,246 --> 00:42:22,081
You also don't know whose car that is?

763
00:42:22,164 --> 00:42:24,708
Something's up with Yang Geum-myeong.
Think about it.

764
00:42:25,376 --> 00:42:26,710
Don't say stuff like that.

765
00:42:27,628 --> 00:42:29,630
She may be poor, but she still has class.

766
00:42:29,713 --> 00:42:32,216
And, Ye-rim,
stop taking her side.

767
00:42:32,299 --> 00:42:35,761
Geum-myeong is never nice to you.
Why give her the benefit of the doubt?

768
00:42:36,345 --> 00:42:37,888
It's how she shows displeasure.

769
00:42:37,972 --> 00:42:39,431
In her own twisted way.

770
00:42:39,515 --> 00:42:41,100
What do you mean?

771
00:42:42,560 --> 00:42:45,563
My dad and I talked a bit about
Geum-myeong the other day.

772
00:42:45,646 --> 00:42:48,899
He said it's a big fish
in a little pond situation.

773
00:42:48,983 --> 00:42:51,652
She's used to being the best
at everything back at home.

774
00:42:51,735 --> 00:42:54,572
However, up here in Seoul,
she's really not that special.

775
00:42:56,156 --> 00:42:58,117
She must feel more inferior every day.

776
00:42:58,784 --> 00:43:01,078
Dad says I should be
the bigger person and let her be.

777
00:43:01,161 --> 00:43:02,454
That's what "class" is.

778
00:43:02,538 --> 00:43:03,372
Okay.

779
00:43:05,374 --> 00:43:07,376
But why would she act that way with you?

780
00:43:08,002 --> 00:43:09,461
Her GPA is higher than yours.

781
00:43:09,545 --> 00:43:11,547
By 0.2. Just by 0.2 points.

782
00:43:11,630 --> 00:43:13,048
- She's taller.
- By two centimeters.

783
00:43:13,132 --> 00:43:14,133
Also,

784
00:43:16,051 --> 00:43:17,886
have you memorized everything about her?

785
00:43:19,054 --> 00:43:20,889
- What do you mean?
- Doesn't matter.

786
00:43:20,973 --> 00:43:22,433
No, tell me. "Doesn't matter" what?

787
00:43:23,434 --> 00:43:24,268
I just meant

788
00:43:25,311 --> 00:43:27,813
Geum-myeong was chosen
to study in Japan first.

789
00:43:27,896 --> 00:43:31,191
If she hadn't passed it up, you wouldn't
have gotten the opportunity. Because of--

790
00:43:31,275 --> 00:43:33,611
If it were up to me,
I'd have chosen her as well.

791
00:43:34,194 --> 00:43:36,113
My family can afford to send me abroad.

792
00:43:36,196 --> 00:43:39,617
It's only natural they would choose
someone from a less fortunate background.

793
00:43:39,700 --> 00:43:40,534
Ye-rim.

794
00:43:40,618 --> 00:43:42,620
Geum-myeong's family is just fine.

795
00:43:42,703 --> 00:43:44,872
- Her father is a captain.
- Of a fishing boat!

796
00:43:44,955 --> 00:43:46,582
Why are you defending her?

797
00:43:48,000 --> 00:43:49,668
That's what class is about.

798
00:43:52,463 --> 00:43:53,422
I'm not hungry.

799
00:43:58,093 --> 00:43:59,762
She dumped you, didn't she?

800
00:43:59,845 --> 00:44:02,264
What is that foreign car?
What is it? Tell me!

801
00:44:03,265 --> 00:44:05,184
You are just dying to know, aren't you?

802
00:44:05,267 --> 00:44:08,771
PRIVATE TUTORING BAN SPARKS ODDITIES
TUTORING EVEN TAKING PLACE IN MOVING CARS!

803
00:44:13,859 --> 00:44:15,694
23RD TYPHOON "PHYLLIS"
CAUTIONS IN FISHING TOWNS

804
00:44:15,778 --> 00:44:17,154
How are the waters today?

805
00:44:18,155 --> 00:44:20,616
No matter how bad
the water might be,

806
00:44:21,200 --> 00:44:22,660
my dad sails to sea.

807
00:44:24,912 --> 00:44:26,830
And it makes me nervous.

808
00:44:28,207 --> 00:44:29,458
- Bye.
- See you later.

809
00:44:29,541 --> 00:44:30,584
Be safe.

810
00:44:39,426 --> 00:44:41,804
- Let's roll.
- No.

811
00:44:41,887 --> 00:44:43,639
- What?
- What did I say about being polite?

812
00:44:43,722 --> 00:44:44,848
Shut the fuck up.

813
00:44:44,932 --> 00:44:47,309
Whoa! Don't say "shut the fuck."
It's "Jesus Christ."

814
00:44:47,393 --> 00:44:48,227
Ugh!

815
00:44:48,310 --> 00:44:51,021
You can't even spell "Wednesday."
Where did you learn to swear?

816
00:44:51,105 --> 00:44:52,439
Jesus!

817
00:44:55,442 --> 00:44:58,237
Jenny, do you know
how to spell "Wednesday"? Write it out.

818
00:44:58,320 --> 00:45:00,030
Write it out.

819
00:45:00,823 --> 00:45:02,574
Oh, goodness gracious.

820
00:45:02,658 --> 00:45:04,410
Why were you named "Jenny" anyway?

821
00:45:04,493 --> 00:45:07,329
Is it to make people think
you're American or something?

822
00:45:07,413 --> 00:45:09,581
If you were anyone else,
I'd have you fired.

823
00:45:09,665 --> 00:45:10,874
I'd have you worse than fired.

824
00:45:10,958 --> 00:45:12,584
Fire me, go ahead.

825
00:45:13,460 --> 00:45:15,337
Why haven't you fired me already?

826
00:45:15,421 --> 00:45:17,506
I heard none of your tutors
last more than a month.

827
00:45:17,589 --> 00:45:19,383
Yeah, I can't wait.

828
00:45:20,342 --> 00:45:21,719
Feet down!

829
00:45:33,772 --> 00:45:34,606
Hey, Jenny.

830
00:45:35,441 --> 00:45:37,401
You didn't memorize the vocab, did you?

831
00:45:38,068 --> 00:45:40,446
You just come to my house to eat,
don't you?

832
00:45:41,363 --> 00:45:44,366
Your housekeeper is good.
She can make food from anywhere.

833
00:45:45,075 --> 00:45:47,119
This is from Busan. Glass noodles.

834
00:45:47,202 --> 00:45:49,872
She just used our money
to impress people.

835
00:45:51,707 --> 00:45:54,710
You're such a brat.
That lady will quit, too, because of you.

836
00:45:55,711 --> 00:45:59,089
That lady has been here the longest.
Mom likes her, I guess.

837
00:46:00,132 --> 00:46:04,219
You know, it seems like people don't stay
at your house for a very long time.

838
00:46:05,053 --> 00:46:05,971
Why?

839
00:46:07,973 --> 00:46:08,891
Why?

840
00:46:11,977 --> 00:46:12,978
Also,

841
00:46:14,521 --> 00:46:18,400
I still don't understand
why I've never met your mother or father.

842
00:46:18,484 --> 00:46:20,319
So what? It's better that way.

843
00:46:20,903 --> 00:46:23,113
I'd like to see their faces at least once.

844
00:46:23,197 --> 00:46:25,657
Well, my mom's seen you.
That should be enough.

845
00:46:25,741 --> 00:46:27,451
What? She saw me? Where?

846
00:46:27,534 --> 00:46:28,619
Where was this?

847
00:46:28,702 --> 00:46:30,454
You stapled a picture to your résumé.

848
00:46:31,079 --> 00:46:34,708
Just hang around until your time's up.
I know you don't wanna be here anyway.

849
00:46:34,792 --> 00:46:36,043
You're here for the money.

850
00:46:36,126 --> 00:46:37,544
Well, aren't you a genius, Jenny.

851
00:46:38,128 --> 00:46:39,963
And, yes, I want to be paid.

852
00:46:40,047 --> 00:46:41,882
Ms. Yang, can't you fix your bangs

853
00:46:41,965 --> 00:46:43,967
or change where
you part your hair at least?

854
00:46:44,051 --> 00:46:45,844
You don't look like you're from Seoul.

855
00:46:46,345 --> 00:46:47,429
Fix them?

856
00:46:47,513 --> 00:46:49,681
Why are you so worried about my hairstyle?

857
00:46:50,390 --> 00:46:53,018
I mean, it's not like
you and I look that much alike.

858
00:46:53,101 --> 00:46:54,019
What?

859
00:46:54,102 --> 00:46:57,064
But… I am the sexier one.

860
00:46:57,147 --> 00:46:59,650
Sexy? Sexy?

861
00:47:00,526 --> 00:47:01,985
Here.

862
00:47:02,069 --> 00:47:04,071
That's a new vocab word. Spell it.

863
00:47:04,154 --> 00:47:06,532
Come on, that's easy. S-E--

864
00:47:06,615 --> 00:47:08,784
Enough.

865
00:47:09,451 --> 00:47:11,078
- S-E…
- I said, enough!

866
00:47:11,161 --> 00:47:12,871
That's all you're interested in, huh?

867
00:47:12,955 --> 00:47:14,998
Little brat, you.

868
00:47:25,884 --> 00:47:28,971
Just take what you're owed.
Don't take more than that.

869
00:47:31,098 --> 00:47:32,808
Your mother is getting to me.

870
00:47:34,142 --> 00:47:36,812
I'm tempted more
every single time, you know.

871
00:47:47,698 --> 00:47:48,782
Hello?

872
00:47:49,366 --> 00:47:50,200
Yeah, what?

873
00:47:50,284 --> 00:47:53,579
Just grab a handful.
Take double for teaching that brat.

874
00:47:55,205 --> 00:47:56,081
What?

875
00:47:59,126 --> 00:48:00,919
Mom's coming. She wants to see you.

876
00:48:01,753 --> 00:48:03,881
- What? Right now?
- Just go.

877
00:48:06,466 --> 00:48:07,467
Go now, girl.

878
00:48:32,951 --> 00:48:36,580
Yes, Ms. Yang,
that's real white porcelain.

879
00:48:38,457 --> 00:48:39,416
I see.

880
00:48:40,459 --> 00:48:42,002
I have everything now.

881
00:48:42,502 --> 00:48:45,047
I have blue porcelain,
and I have white as well.

882
00:48:45,839 --> 00:48:48,759
Everything.
Everything except a good education.

883
00:48:50,385 --> 00:48:51,803
W… wow.

884
00:48:51,887 --> 00:48:54,556
I have such deep regret
for my lack of education.

885
00:48:54,640 --> 00:48:56,850
I was hoping to be able
to live through my daughter,

886
00:48:56,934 --> 00:48:59,186
but she has my intellect, unfortunately.

887
00:49:02,314 --> 00:49:06,360
We'll raise her grades little by little.
Don't worry.

888
00:49:06,443 --> 00:49:08,487
Sadly, there's no time for that now.

889
00:49:09,237 --> 00:49:11,448
Life doesn't wait for anyone.
We all know that.

890
00:49:12,616 --> 00:49:13,450
Ah…

891
00:49:13,951 --> 00:49:17,245
Uh, then does that mean I'm fired?

892
00:49:17,329 --> 00:49:19,873
Jenny is very wealthy,
but she isn't that clever,

893
00:49:19,957 --> 00:49:22,626
while you are very smart
and not much else.

894
00:49:22,709 --> 00:49:24,670
So let's try work this out together.

895
00:49:26,296 --> 00:49:29,466
I'll set things up
and take care of everything.

896
00:49:29,549 --> 00:49:31,802
You just follow my lead and directions.

897
00:49:32,594 --> 00:49:35,931
It took us two years to find a tutor
that looked like our daughter.

898
00:49:36,014 --> 00:49:37,641
Her college exams are very soon.

899
00:49:38,225 --> 00:49:39,685
You should take the exams for her.

900
00:49:40,394 --> 00:49:42,729
That's what I'm demanding of you,
Ms. Yang.

901
00:49:54,783 --> 00:49:55,617
Uh…

902
00:49:57,119 --> 00:49:58,620
Uh…

903
00:50:01,248 --> 00:50:03,625
STUDENT ID
OH JENNY

904
00:50:03,709 --> 00:50:05,085
TEST IDENTIFICATION SLIP
OH JENNY

905
00:50:05,168 --> 00:50:07,504
If she gets into a top-three university,

906
00:50:07,587 --> 00:50:10,007
I'll buy you a 1,300-square-foot apartment

907
00:50:10,090 --> 00:50:12,592
and a 1,000-square-foot one
for other colleges.

908
00:50:20,976 --> 00:50:23,145
NOTICE
LIST OF APPROVED APPLICANTS FOR DORMS

909
00:50:25,188 --> 00:50:28,066
If her name
isn't here, she can't live in the dorms?

910
00:50:28,775 --> 00:50:29,776
No.

911
00:50:31,653 --> 00:50:33,864
Then a boarding house.

912
00:50:35,365 --> 00:50:36,575
How much is the rent there?

913
00:50:38,660 --> 00:50:39,578
A lot.

914
00:50:40,579 --> 00:50:41,913
It'll be expensive.

915
00:51:08,648 --> 00:51:09,483
What?

916
00:51:10,233 --> 00:51:11,359
Is he trying to fight?

917
00:51:12,152 --> 00:51:14,071
<i>The eyes of the world</i>
<i>are upon us</i>

918
00:51:14,154 --> 00:51:18,366
<i>as a historical presidential election</i>
<i>unfolds today, on December 16th.</i>

919
00:51:18,867 --> 00:51:20,911
<i>It has been 16 years since our citizens</i>

920
00:51:20,994 --> 00:51:23,288
<i>have been able</i>
<i>to directly vote for the president.</i>

921
00:51:23,371 --> 00:51:24,664
<i>The atmosphere is solemn.</i>

922
00:51:25,707 --> 00:51:30,253
They say the dorm selection is by lottery,
but I think there are backdoor deals.

923
00:51:30,337 --> 00:51:33,924
We all know supposedly
"clean" organizations can be shady.

924
00:51:34,007 --> 00:51:34,841
Right?

925
00:51:34,925 --> 00:51:36,343
<i>…president of their choice.</i>

926
00:51:36,426 --> 00:51:39,221
So… who are you voting for?

927
00:51:39,304 --> 00:51:41,348
<i>…government has declared today</i>
<i>a temporary…</i>

928
00:51:41,431 --> 00:51:43,809
I think we need to call
the military police.

929
00:51:43,892 --> 00:51:44,768
Excuse me?

930
00:51:44,851 --> 00:51:47,521
Why is there
a soldier outside the girls' dorm?

931
00:51:48,021 --> 00:51:49,523
The guys' dorms are nearby.

932
00:51:50,524 --> 00:51:53,360
Usually, when there's a break,
they come in and out.

933
00:51:55,862 --> 00:51:56,988
So who'd you vote for?

934
00:51:57,489 --> 00:51:59,950
<i>…had given their all</i>
<i>to ask for each of their votes.</i>

935
00:52:00,033 --> 00:52:02,285
You think they will be able
to arrest that guy?

936
00:52:07,249 --> 00:52:08,125
One.

937
00:52:08,667 --> 00:52:10,335
One, two, three.

938
00:52:11,461 --> 00:52:12,379
Oh!

939
00:52:16,925 --> 00:52:18,385
Sir, good to meet you again.

940
00:52:24,266 --> 00:52:27,060
Remember me, sir?
We met at the admission ceremony.

941
00:52:27,144 --> 00:52:29,729
I'm Park Yeong-beom,
and your daughter and I,

942
00:52:30,230 --> 00:52:31,148
we are friends.

943
00:52:36,987 --> 00:52:41,241
I recall on that day, I actually took
a few pictures of you guys.

944
00:52:45,453 --> 00:52:48,206
You were saying how
you took a plane to see Geum-myeong,

945
00:52:48,790 --> 00:52:49,875
then you took a bus.

946
00:52:50,375 --> 00:52:51,334
Yeah.

947
00:52:51,418 --> 00:52:52,460
What kind of friend?

948
00:52:53,336 --> 00:52:55,130
- Sir?
- I asked you a question.

949
00:52:56,506 --> 00:52:58,216
- Yeah?
- You're a friend of my daughter.

950
00:52:58,300 --> 00:53:00,594
Well, so tell me,
what kind of friend are you, boy?

951
00:53:00,677 --> 00:53:02,012
{\an8}TEST IDENTIFICATION SLIP
OH JENNY

952
00:53:02,095 --> 00:53:02,929
{\an8}Oh my God.

953
00:53:04,389 --> 00:53:06,057
Oh.

954
00:53:06,141 --> 00:53:07,726
I'm sorry, ma'am.

955
00:53:07,809 --> 00:53:09,895
This seems kind of risky.

956
00:53:09,978 --> 00:53:11,438
Tutoring is already illegal.

957
00:53:11,521 --> 00:53:14,441
In fact, every time I come here,
I get nervous.

958
00:53:14,983 --> 00:53:17,986
Takes nerve to earn
any money in this world, dear.

959
00:53:18,528 --> 00:53:20,822
You can't win if you risk nothing at all.

960
00:53:20,906 --> 00:53:22,949
If I get caught, I'd be expelled.

961
00:53:23,033 --> 00:53:25,035
That's why you're getting an apartment,

962
00:53:25,118 --> 00:53:27,829
to compensate you
for the risk of expulsion.

963
00:53:29,581 --> 00:53:32,250
Hold on, this exam is serious.

964
00:53:32,334 --> 00:53:34,336
You really think I can be Jenny?

965
00:53:35,212 --> 00:53:38,840
Whoever the proctor is,
I'll have greased their palm.

966
00:53:38,924 --> 00:53:41,593
I will arrange everything for you nicely

967
00:53:41,676 --> 00:53:44,054
so you won't have a reason
to be worried at all.

968
00:53:46,014 --> 00:53:50,602
Doesn't everyone make their money
by doing what they're good at?

969
00:53:50,685 --> 00:53:53,146
I will assist you
by doing what I'm good at.

970
00:53:54,022 --> 00:53:57,525
Isn't it right and honorable
to make a living using your talents?

971
00:53:58,735 --> 00:54:01,905
Just turn a blind eye this once
and take the apartment.

972
00:54:04,950 --> 00:54:06,243
There's just one thing--

973
00:54:06,326 --> 00:54:07,244
No, dear.

974
00:54:08,036 --> 00:54:09,746
I don't wanna hear it.

975
00:54:10,330 --> 00:54:14,251
Before you speak, think carefully about
what you stand to lose.

976
00:54:20,382 --> 00:54:24,010
You're running out of scholarship money,
and you have to leave the dorms.

977
00:54:24,511 --> 00:54:26,429
Forget about studying abroad.

978
00:54:26,513 --> 00:54:29,015
How… do you know all that?

979
00:54:29,516 --> 00:54:31,434
As I said, think carefully.

980
00:54:32,060 --> 00:54:37,023
Think of your parents who worked so hard
to get you to where you are, Ms. Yang.

981
00:54:37,107 --> 00:54:40,652
You're a fish
trying to get out of her pond,

982
00:54:41,152 --> 00:54:44,114
but that pond is getting dry. Hmm?

983
00:54:46,658 --> 00:54:47,784
Follow me.

984
00:54:48,785 --> 00:54:50,870
Hey. Go to your room.

985
00:54:56,918 --> 00:54:58,086
Young lady!

986
00:54:58,962 --> 00:55:00,297
Hey, young lady!

987
00:55:00,380 --> 00:55:01,840
Hey, young lady!

988
00:55:01,923 --> 00:55:02,924
Oh my.

989
00:55:03,842 --> 00:55:05,760
Did you just leave unit 908?

990
00:55:06,261 --> 00:55:08,346
Yes? What's this about?

991
00:55:08,430 --> 00:55:09,973
You ran so fast,

992
00:55:10,056 --> 00:55:12,100
I wasn't able to catch up.

993
00:55:12,684 --> 00:55:14,185
What? Why would I run?

994
00:55:14,269 --> 00:55:15,895
You stole something from that family?

995
00:55:16,521 --> 00:55:17,355
Huh?

996
00:55:18,231 --> 00:55:21,609
Come. Just give it here.
Don't make any more trouble.

997
00:55:24,571 --> 00:55:26,865
Um, is that what she said?

998
00:55:29,034 --> 00:55:31,619
I don't need
an answer from you right now.

999
00:55:32,287 --> 00:55:33,830
Just take these with you.

1000
00:55:35,415 --> 00:55:38,835
Look at it as many times as you need,
then tell me your decision, okay?

1001
00:55:40,003 --> 00:55:42,714
Nobody wants to be stuck
in a small pond, do they?

1002
00:55:42,797 --> 00:55:45,300
It's just too sad to contemplate.

1003
00:55:46,176 --> 00:55:47,052
Imagine, instead,

1004
00:55:47,135 --> 00:55:50,138
how you'd be able to give
your mother and father the whole world.

1005
00:55:50,221 --> 00:55:53,558
That poor father of yours.
Always riding his boat.

1006
00:55:54,142 --> 00:55:56,853
He'll have to ride in that boat
for the rest of his life.

1007
00:56:00,482 --> 00:56:01,566
I remember my father.

1008
00:56:02,192 --> 00:56:04,944
He trusted his eldest son to pass the bar,

1009
00:56:05,028 --> 00:56:08,031
and he was stuck tending his cows
until the day he died.

1010
00:56:09,949 --> 00:56:12,619
When I think of my parents
and how they're struggling,

1011
00:56:12,702 --> 00:56:14,579
there's nothing to think about here.

1012
00:56:14,662 --> 00:56:17,916
What's better than earning an apartment
doing what I'm good at?

1013
00:56:18,416 --> 00:56:20,543
Yes, that's what I wanna hear.

1014
00:56:20,627 --> 00:56:22,837
I remember what my mom and dad taught me.

1015
00:56:23,421 --> 00:56:24,255
What?

1016
00:56:24,339 --> 00:56:27,717
I was taught it was better to fail a class
than cheat my way in.

1017
00:56:28,385 --> 00:56:32,013
I was taught not to take money I found
but to report it instead.

1018
00:56:32,097 --> 00:56:35,892
I know my parents wouldn't want me to live
as a fraud or a scammer.

1019
00:56:35,975 --> 00:56:39,104
Huh? What exactly
are you trying to say to me?

1020
00:56:39,187 --> 00:56:40,230
Just

1021
00:56:40,814 --> 00:56:43,858
that if I take the test
and Jenny gets accepted somehow,

1022
00:56:43,942 --> 00:56:45,819
then a girl like me won't, and

1023
00:56:46,778 --> 00:56:49,280
I can't stand the idea
of taking it from her.

1024
00:56:50,323 --> 00:56:51,991
If she found out about it,

1025
00:56:52,742 --> 00:56:54,285
she would die of heartbreak.

1026
00:56:55,161 --> 00:56:57,122
Yang Geum-myeong, listen to me.

1027
00:56:57,789 --> 00:56:59,916
It's one thing
to stand for your principles

1028
00:56:59,999 --> 00:57:01,751
when you have the proper means,

1029
00:57:01,835 --> 00:57:05,004
but to do it when you have nothing
is simply recklessness.

1030
00:57:05,088 --> 00:57:06,965
I'd say sending a girl
who can't even spell

1031
00:57:07,048 --> 00:57:08,675
to an elite school would be reckless.

1032
00:57:08,758 --> 00:57:10,593
Would you?

1033
00:57:12,554 --> 00:57:13,721
I think you

1034
00:57:14,347 --> 00:57:16,349
should let Jenny find out
what she's really good at.

1035
00:57:17,183 --> 00:57:19,769
Isn't that the right and honorable thing
to do for Jenny?

1036
00:57:20,728 --> 00:57:22,188
Yeah, I'd rather be a singer.

1037
00:57:27,318 --> 00:57:28,570
I am leaving now.

1038
00:57:28,653 --> 00:57:33,158
All you little fish
are exactly the same.

1039
00:57:33,658 --> 00:57:35,285
You have nothing to your name,

1040
00:57:35,368 --> 00:57:39,372
so all you have to live for is preserving
your pathetic sense of pride!

1041
00:57:41,708 --> 00:57:43,460
Jenny was always a pain in the ass.

1042
00:57:46,713 --> 00:57:48,798
I think I deserve a raise after all this.

1043
00:58:06,149 --> 00:58:07,734
You know I'm not a thief.

1044
00:58:07,817 --> 00:58:10,612
Oh yes, I know.
I'm just keeping out of that bully's way.

1045
00:58:10,695 --> 00:58:13,156
All the cash in the world
can't buy my integrity.

1046
00:58:16,701 --> 00:58:17,535
The ring?

1047
00:58:18,286 --> 00:58:19,120
What?

1048
00:58:19,204 --> 00:58:21,456
You know, the diamond ring.

1049
00:58:35,970 --> 00:58:37,889
<i>My parents always hoped…</i>

1050
00:58:38,890 --> 00:58:43,186
<i>…that away from their arms,</i>
<i>my life would be rosy, easy, and carefree.</i>

1051
00:58:43,269 --> 00:58:44,604
Open up!

1052
00:58:46,189 --> 00:58:47,482
Ma'am, open up!

1053
00:58:48,274 --> 00:58:51,069
Hey, Jenny! Open the door, come on!

1054
00:58:51,152 --> 00:58:52,862
I didn't steal anything!

1055
00:58:54,531 --> 00:58:58,618
Hey! You know I'm not a thief! Open up!

1056
00:58:59,619 --> 00:59:02,705
<i>But the truth is,</i>
<i>the world away from their arms</i>

1057
00:59:03,331 --> 00:59:04,374
<i>was a jungle.</i>

1058
01:01:51,541 --> 01:01:55,545
"IN THE HOPE THAT OUR ECHOES
WILL FLOW AND FLOW, UNTIL THEY REACH YOU."

